Z||000000||BroCar 87||02-06-2001||12:08 AM||||OK call me a dreamer, but I was wondering if I went ahead and got my V8 up and running, would it be TOO much to add a supercharger? I mean I know I couldn't ever nail the gas pedal (fear of breaking the tranny) but if I have to be careful as it is (JUST by running a V8) couldn't I just go all out and just HAVE a supercharged v8 fiero?<BR>Anyone have any comments or suggestions?<BR>BroCar 87||||reg||6
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||02-06-2001||12:58 AM||||I suggest you drive the car with the V8 first.  If you really think it is still not powerful enough, then I guess you should put a supercharger on it.<P>I suspect the first time you "try out" your V8 conversion it will impress you enough to answer this question inequivocally.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||02-06-2001||02:10 AM||||OHH Lucky, I know the V8 will astonish me by al means, but I was wondering since I already have to be careful on the throttle, would it be too much power if I did add a supercharger. I would say at 6#'s of boost. Powerdyne Superchargers are pretty much bolt up and go type chargers. I would like to just have to the title of SUPERCHARGED V8 FIERO. That was going on in head this entire day.<BR>Anyone think it would be too much. Not even worth the money???<BR>Thanks for your input Lucky...<BR>BroCar 87||||reg||6
