Z||000007||BBBAD GT||02-07-2001||09:25 AM||||Are you going with a carbed or fuel injected V8?  A blower on a carb has/can work, its not as easy to tune as a fuel injected motor, and I still don't know how flexable the fuel injection of chevy's are with blowers.  Everybody like slapping on blowers/turbos, but if you can't tune it right, then you'll be asking yourself why you went that route.  <P>BUT, having that all cleared up, sounds like a fun ride  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||10:11 AM||||nitrous is cheaper and you'll still be able to drive the car... if you want the killer whine that a roots type makes get cut idler-gears. I have been fortunate and been able to drive BBBads V8 uum it's PLENTY of go and it's only got 200hp.. but it's a torque MONSTER! <P>just my $.02||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shaun41178||02-07-2001||06:30 PM||||yea go with nitrous.  you can adjust that to like 200 hp or so on demand to give that extra kick in the butt.  plus it will be cheaper to add and give normal driving around town.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
